  "term": "strings",
  "says": "Reid's bowed-string section: saws (the bowed string's slip-stick is a saw) with several slightly detuned copies for the ensemble, a low-pass that takes off the fizz but leaves the bow's brightness, an attack of a tenth to half a second (the bow has to get the string going), a matching release, a slow vibrato on the whole. Signature: harmonic, some stereo width from the ensemble, a centroid in the mids, an attack well above a keyboard's, a steady level once the note is up. Measured 2026-09-14: 'a steady level' was refuted - five copies detuned by a few cents beat by 2.5 dB over the held note (3.8 dB at a wider detune), and that beating is the ensemble; the entry now expects it, between 0.5 and 5 dB.",
